:: Rude Awakening {"position":"450,200","size":"100,100"}

The sound of metal clinking is the first, fuzzy sensation that breaks through the void of forced stasis. It's a gentle sound like the chime of a tuning fork during temple service.  Your optics are slow to online, despite your sole focus being drawn to the sound. Eventually the sound disappears just before your optics fully come online, visual feed still fuzzy with static.

You're on your backplates staring straight up at a garish orange-bronze ceiling. You think, at once, that it's quite ugly and not at all like the metal interiors you're used to. It's 'unfinished': bolts bare to the naked optic and metal unpolished, showing a fine collection of dirt across its once shiny surface. Very utilitarian.

"Oh, good. You're awake. You gave us quite a scare when you didn't immediately online," A white mech--a medic, you think--comes into view. Just as utilitarian in form as the ceiling he's under. What startles you to full awareness is just how **boxy** this mech is. His frame is like yours but not like yours. In fact, not like any mech you've ever seen. You startle up onto your forearms, giving the medic a once over as he tries to ease you back into a lying position.

"Who are you talking to, Ratch? Are they awake?" Another mech, in deep green armor, comes up behind this strange medic. Oh, he's just as boxy if not moreso! You scramble back on the metal slab, trying to pull as far away from this strange medic's servos as possible.

You see a series of medical instruments just off to the side. Among them what you think must be a scalple.

[[Grab a weapon]]

[[Scramble off the berth]]

:: Grab a weapon {"position":"575,275","size":"100,100"}
<<set $mcDominant += 1>> <kinktext>Dominance +1</kinktext>

You see that horrible red face on their armor--twin to the harbinger of death--and you waste no time in grabbing a weapon. You hold the tool between you and the white medic, glaring defiantly between one and then the other.

"Don't touch me!" You carefully move back on the medical slab until you can feel the edge, cautiously lowering one pede to the floor and then the other. The white medic puts up his servos in a placating gesture, his optics never leaving your face even when you make a motion like you will lunge at him. He pointedly ignores the laser scalple in your grasp.

"We're not going to hurt you," You scoff at his words, optics never leaving the two mechs in front of you. You don't know if you have the werewithal to actually use the meager weapon in your servo, but you're definitely not letting these monsters lay one digit on you.





[[Keep the newcomer at bay]]

:: Scramble off the berth {"position":"575,150","size":"100,100"}
<<set $mcSubmissive += 1>> <kinktext>Submissiveness +1</kinktext>

You hastily pull yourself off the medical table, slipping as you get one pede on the floor and tumbling down chassis first. The medic immediately comes around to try to help you, cursing all the while, but you don't hesitate to continue moving. You put as much space--as quickly as you can--between you and your kidnappers, speeding to tbe other end of the room and ducking behind another of the medical slabs.

"Who are you? Where have you taken me?" You eye them warily, tring to keep both of them in your field of view. So preoccupied with getting distance between you and these strangers, you almost miss the red face emblazoned proudly upon their metal. Stark and bright. A close brother to that mark of evil. Dread makes your pauldrons hunch all the way up to your audials. How did you end up in their servos?

"It's okay, just calm down," The green mech speaks through his face covering, tone too gentle and cheery for your liking, "We're not going to hurt you."

You don't believe them in the least. Unfortunately, there's so many doors in this room that you're not sure which one leads **out**.

Before you can come up with a plan, one of them opens to reveal a __large__ blue and red bot.
	<<if $height=["giant"]>> But not as large as you.
	<<elseif $height=["large]>> About the same size as you. Maybe you can still take him.
	<<elseif $height=["average","small","mini"]>> Larger than you. You may not be able to threaten your way out of this.
	<</if>>

